## Groups as Project Types

You're right that `agent_group_definitions` should own this. A group isn't "agents that work together" - it's a **project recipe**:

```
group: landing-page-builder
  → briefer → strategist → landing-architect → content-creator → assembler → git-deployer
  → outputs: single index.html

group: content-site-builder
  → briefer → strategist → content-architect → content-creator → multi-page-assembler → git-deployer
  → outputs: index.html, article-template.html, category pages, shared partials

group: static-blog-builder (future)
  → briefer → strategist → 11ty-architect → content-creator → build-runner → git-deployer
  → outputs: 11ty project structure, builds to static files

group: ecommerce-builder (future)
  → briefer → strategist → storefront-architect → product-creator → cart-assembler → k8s-deployer
  → outputs: frontend + backend + database schema
```

Shared agents: `briefer`, `content-creator` (writes copy regardless of output format)
Specialized agents: architects, assemblers, deployers vary by group

